From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0038] STEAMAC-3Q Reject unsupported texel buffer formats before Metal

STEAMAC-3Q and development reports STEAMAC-46/47 abort in
MVKDevice::getVkFormatTexelBufferAlignment from vkCreateBufferView. STEAMAC-46
records Metal's always-on assertion: MTLPixelFormatInvalid is not supported
on this device. Vulkan applications can pass RGB formats that have no Metal
pixel representation (and advertise no texel-buffer format features).

Reject unsupported buffer-view formats with VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED
before alignment queries or texel arithmetic. The existing Vulkan entry point
clears the returned handle and destroys the failed view.
Check advertised texel-buffer capabilities before converting the format: the
conversion error path appends a format name, which is null for unknown enums.
Report rejected formats numerically so unknown values also fail cleanly.

The alignment helper also serves image construction. Return the existing
fallback alignment without querying Metal for unsupported or non-linear
formats, checking the selected Metal plane to retain multi-planar alignment.
Supported linear formats still obtain their device-specific alignment.

Regression coverage: host/moltenvk/repro/texel_buffer.c --format <case>, with
Metal API validation enabled. RGB32, RGB16, undefined/unknown, depth,
compressed and YCbCr formats must fail cleanly; R32/R8/RGBA8 controls succeed.
The ordinary texel-buffer repro also runs all format-creation cases.

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm
@@ -304,11 +304,24 @@
 	MVKPixelFormats* pixFmts = getPixelFormats();
     _buffer = (MVKBuffer*)pCreateInfo->buffer;
     _offset = pCreateInfo->offset;
-    _mtlPixelFormat = pixFmts->getMTLPixelFormat(pCreateInfo->format);
+	// Check capabilities before format conversion: unknown VkFormats have no diagnostic name.
+	VkFormatFeatureFlags2 formatFeatures = pixFmts->getVkFormatProperties3(pCreateInfo->format).bufferFeatures;
+	_mtlPixelFormat = mvkIsAnyFlagEnabled(formatFeatures,
+										VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_UNIFORM_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT | VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_2_STORAGE_TEXEL_BUFFER_BIT)
+						? pixFmts->getMTLPixelFormat(pCreateInfo->format) : MTLPixelFormatInvalid;
     VkExtent2D fmtBlockSize = pixFmts->getBlockTexelSize(pCreateInfo->format);  // Pixel size of format
     size_t bytesPerBlock = pixFmts->getBytesPerBlock(pCreateInfo->format);
 	_bytesPerPixel = static_cast<uint32_t>(bytesPerBlock);
 	_mtlTexture = nil;
+
+	// Games can request formats with no Metal texel-buffer representation (e.g. RGB32).
+	// Reject them before offset/size arithmetic or Metal's always-on alignment validation.
+	if (!_mtlPixelFormat || !bytesPerBlock) {
+		setConfigurationResult(reportError(VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED,
+										   "vkCreateBufferView(): Format %d does not support texel buffers on this device.",
+										   pCreateInfo->format));
+		return;
+	}
 	auto& mtlFeats = getMetalFeatures();
 
 	if (mtlFeats.emulatedTexelBufferAlignment) {
diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.mm
@@ -4968,6 +4968,15 @@
 		// typically have stricter alignment requirements due to it being a 2-component format.
 		mtlPixFmt = mvkPixFmts->getChromaSubsamplingPlaneMTLPixelFormat(format, 1);
 	}
+	// Metal asserts for invalid/unsupported formats, rather than returning zero.
+	// This helper is also used while configuring images, including rejected linear images.
+	// Check the selected plane's Metal format so valid multi-planar images retain their alignment.
+	VkExtent2D blockSize = mvkPixFmts->getBlockTexelSize(mtlPixFmt);
+	if (!mvkPixFmts->isSupported(mtlPixFmt) ||
+		mvkPixFmts->isDepthFormat(mtlPixFmt) || mvkPixFmts->isStencilFormat(mtlPixFmt) ||
+		blockSize.width != 1 || blockSize.height != 1) {
+		return _physicalDevice->_properties.limits.minTexelBufferOffsetAlignment;
+	}
 	deviceAlignment = [mtlDev minimumLinearTextureAlignmentForPixelFormat: mtlPixFmt];
 
 	return deviceAlignment ? deviceAlignment : _physicalDevice->_properties.limits.minTexelBufferOffsetAlignment;
